msgid "advice.*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/advice.txt:7
msgid ""
"These variables control various optional help messages designed to aid new "
"users.  When left unconfigured, Git will give the message alongside "
"instructions on how to squelch it.  You can tell Git that you have "
"understood the issue and no longer need a specific help message by setting "
"the corresponding variable to `false`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/advice.txt:12
msgid ""
"As they are intended to help human users, these messages are output to the "
"standard error. When tools that run Git as a subprocess find them "
"disruptive, they can set `GIT_ADVICE=0` in the environment to squelch all "
"advice messages."
msgstr ""

